# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch C."""
DESC_C = {
    "RT": {
        62: "A Drifand piloted by Maaie.\nThe Moraba was developed in the 17th year of the Chaotic Era for purposes such as escorting factories, and stands as a pioneering example of Emaan devices.\nIts simple structure makes it easy to modify, resulting in numerous derivative variants depending on the factory operating it or the pilot flying it. Its shoulders and arms can also be folded in to reduce air resistance.\nMaaie's unit is a relatively standard, lightly armed type equipped with a five-barrel Gatling Cannon and a Grenade Gun, and it excels in maneuverability and mobility.",
        63: "A Drifand piloted by Lieea. Kei also rode in it once.\nWhere Maaie's unit is close to the standard type, Lieea's has been extensively modified in terms of armament. Though ill-suited to high-mobility combat, it boasts increased firepower thanks to equipment such as a large Missile Gun pod, a grenade launcher, and a missile guidance system, and it excels at hit-and-run tactics.\nThe Moraba is also equipped with the sympathetic response system later adapted for use in the Orguss as well. By transmitting the pilot's thoughts directly to the machine, it allows reflexive movement even in situations where mechanical piloting alone could not react in time. Thanks to this system, even an inexperienced pilot can manage a certain degree of combat.",
        64: "A second-generation Gerwalk (biped) weapon used by the Freedom Space Corps, the faction to which Kei and Olson belonged.\nBesides high-speed combat in Flyer Form, it can also fight on the ground in Gerwalk Form. Its legs serve not only as landing gear but also house thrusters at their base that boost propulsion during flight.\nThough it has no arms, a manipulator is built into the lower torso, allowing for fine work. Kei used this manipulator to activate an unadjusted space-time oscillation bomb, an accident that sent him and the Bronco II flying twenty years into the future, into the Chaotic Era.",
        65: "A commercial vessel built for Emaan people to conduct trade wherever they travel. The factory led by Shaya also makes use of this ship.\nIts exterior, with a red roof and white walls, looks exactly like a house out of a storybook. The resemblance goes beyond appearance too - wooden furnishings and landscape paintings decorate its interior, and it is even equipped with sports facilities and a public-bath-style bathing area, giving it a strong sense of being a living space for the factory's crew. Even so, it also houses mecha hangars and workshops capable of repair and assembly.\nThe Chiram call it by the code name 'House.'",
        66: "A reconnaissance variant of the Ishkick. Model number RSG-21A-1.\nThough it uses the same legs as the Ishkick, its cockpit is a vertically stacked two-seater, with an operator on top and a pilot below, securing a wide field of view.\nTo avoid detection by enemy craft, its propulsion system is built with excellent sound and infrared suppression. It also mounts a compact reactor with a quiet drive despite its low output, among various other features tailored to its role as a reconnaissance craft.",
        67: "A third-generation combat device developed by the Chiram military to establish a new weapons system suited to the chaos-torn world. Model number MBG-21D-2.\nIt is a legged fighter of the type commonly called Gerwalk in Chiram weaponry, and it appears to be produced in enormous numbers as a mainline unit. It incorporates the new anti-gravity system technology, which, while limiting its top speed, greatly improves its mobility.\nIts firepower is formidable, combining a large-caliber Beam Cannon on the front of the fuselage with sixteen loaded Missiles. The ultra-thick steel plating used on the front of its legs serves double duty, both for inertial maneuvering and as a blunt weapon in close combat.",
        68: "A commander-type Ishkick modified for use by unit commanders. Model number MBG-21F-1.\nIt adds an abundance of weaponry, including a 90mm rapid-fire grenade cannon, a large-caliber Beam Cannon with adjustable output, and 20mm twin AutoGuns, along with an advanced detection system.\nIts full loaded weight approaches the 30-ton carrying limit, and although auxiliary Boosters have been fitted to ease the load on its legs, its operational time is still considerably shortened. It is also difficult to pilot, causing problems that can hinder mission operations, among other issues. Even so, it remains popular among confident commanders and continues to see frontline use.",
        69: "A further-modified version of the commander-type Ishkick, itself already a commander conversion of the standard Ishkick.\nIncidentally, Chiram devices can be identified by their name suffix: those ending in 'Kick' are combat models, while those ending in 'Fone' are reconnaissance models.",
        70: "Athena Henderson's personal Nikick. As a commander-type unit, model number MBG-24C, it differs from the type piloted by regular soldiers in both head shape and body color.\nAthena's unit carries a Triple Shot Cannon as its sidearm, a flashier weapon than the single-shot Laser pistol used on Olson's unit.",
        71: "Olson D. Verne's personal Nikick. As a commander-type unit, model number MBG-24C, it differs from the type piloted by regular soldiers in both head shape and body color.\nIts armament consists of napalm Missiles mounted on the legs, a Beam Cannon at the waist, and a single-shot Laser pistol.",
        72: "A fourth-generation combat device developed by the Chiram military to counter the Mu. This is the standard type piloted by regular soldiers, model number MBG-24A.\nTo handle a variety of combat situations single-handedly, it has a variable-form function allowing it to take three forms: Battle Form, Flyer Form, and Gerwalk Form.\nCompared to the Ishkick, it has twice the mass and six times the output, making it quite a heavyweight machine by Chiram standards, with performance nearly on par with the Orguss. It is likewise capable of inertial control, but since much of its inertial control system remains underdeveloped, it is less reliable than the Orguss in this regard.",
        73: "An attack carrier operated by the Chiram military.\nIt carries numerous combat devices and has ten silos built into its deck for launching Large Missiles.\nIts interior also houses a conference room where officers of command rank gather.",
        74: "Emaan's main battleship, operated as the mothership of the Dimora.\nIt was later repurposed as a carrier for the Orguss II as well, and can hold six units in Gerwalk form.",
        75: "A Drifand used by Emaan. It can be equipped with the same type of Missile Gun and missile pack used on the Orguss, and it saw extensive use in Manisha's unit as well.\nEmaan devices are fitted with an Inertial Control System capable of negating the mass of matter. This eliminates the effects of gravity, allowing for easy rapid acceleration, sudden stops, and sharp turns, while also reducing the G-forces exerted on the pilot to almost nothing. Thanks to this benefit, the machine can operate under nearly any conditions, so long as air resistance is taken into account.\nAs various manipulators were developed to improve work efficiency and combat capability, this eventually led to the arms it carries today. This is why it is called a Drifand, short for 'Drift Hand.'",
        76: "A large Walker Machine created by the Innocent, a high-performance unit capable of movement nearly indistinguishable from a human's. It conceals a separation-and-combination mechanism linking two mecha, as well as a transformation function into a linked car form.\nIts outstanding mobility and output, along with its wide array of optional weaponry, all far surpass those of conventional Walker Machines.\nIts drawback is poor maintainability stemming from the complexity of its mechanisms. Even Cattset's skill reportedly struggled with it - there were malfunctions where, after transforming, the head would get stuck and fail to emerge.\nTwo units existed. One had its wings destroyed by Jiron, rendering it unable to transform, and it was thereafter operated as the Sub Xabungle. It was later destroyed in battle against the Greta Gully.",
        77: "The most advanced large Walker Machine created by the Innocent. After losing the Xabungle, Jiron seized this unit and operated it aboard the Iron Gear from then on.\nWhile matching the Xabungle in mobility, it is improved across the board in maneuverability, armor, and firepower. The combination mechanism that was the Xabungle's greatest weak point has been greatly simplified in this unit, resulting in an all-around machine with excellent maintainability as well.\nIts firepower is high, thanks to dedicated weapons such as the Boomerang Idiom and a five-tube rocket launcher, along with a Bazooka wrested away from the female warrior Tron. It also possesses powerful hover capability, allowing for standalone flight, though not with complete freedom of movement.",
        78: "The first of three landships built to the Iron Gear type. Its greatest feature is its ability to transform into Walker Machine form.\nProvided by the Innocent to Elche's father, Kyarin, it possesses overwhelming combat power. On the other hand, it is something of a prototype vessel, with lingering issues in fuel efficiency and maintainability, frequently breaking down and infuriating Cattset, who handles its piloting and upkeep.\nThe original Iron Gear was badly damaged in battle against its sister ship, the second Iron Gear-type vessel, the Greta Gully. Even so, it won that battle, and by capturing the Greta Gully and repainting it, it has been put into service as the second-generation Iron Gear.",
        79: "The state of the Iron Gear transformed into Walker Machine form.\nThe transformation mechanism from landship to Walker Machine is fitted only to the Iron Gear type, and its combat strength is unmatched by anything else. That said, this comes at a considerable cost to the airframe. There are also numerous points that could stand improvement, such as a major drop in mobility and a lack of means to attack targets to its rear.\nSurprisingly, it is also dexterous, having even been seen untying, on its own, the knot of the head-wrap it wore as snowfield camouflage.\nDespite its massive size, it is capable of soaring high into the air and diving down to attack. Its offensive power is unrivaled, but if cargo aboard is not secured, considerable damage inside the ship can be expected.",
        80: "A small Walker Machine that could be called suited for beginners.\nEasy to pilot and inexpensive, with enough all-around versatility to handle most kinds of work, it was the machine that sparked the widespread popularity of Walker Machines.",
        81: "A small Walker Machine that could be called suited for beginners.\nEasy to pilot and inexpensive, with enough all-around versatility to handle most kinds of work, it was the machine that sparked the widespread popularity of Walker Machines.",
        82: "A well-balanced, large Walker Machine.\nThough it falls short of machines specialized for particular tasks, it can be used for a wide range of purposes, from mining and hauling cargo to combat, making it the most widely used machine of its kind.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        83: "A well-balanced, large Walker Machine.\nThough it falls short of machines specialized for particular tasks, it can be used for a wide range of purposes, from mining and hauling cargo to combat, making it the most widely used machine of its kind.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        84: "A well-balanced, large Walker Machine.\nThough it falls short of machines specialized for particular tasks, it can be used for a wide range of purposes, from mining and hauling cargo to combat, making it the most widely used machine of its kind.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        85: "A well-balanced, large Walker Machine.\nThough it falls short of machines specialized for particular tasks, it can be used for a wide range of purposes, from mining and hauling cargo to combat, making it the most widely used machine of its kind.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        86: "A humanoid Walker Machine developed in the relatively early stages.\nAlthough its joints are somewhat fragile, its light weight makes it easy to handle, giving it excellent mobility and maneuverability. It also readily accepts optional parts and can easily be loaded onto a landship for transport, making it an overall high-performance machine.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        87: "A humanoid Walker Machine developed in the relatively early stages.\nAlthough its joints are somewhat fragile, its light weight makes it easy to handle, giving it excellent mobility and maneuverability. It also readily accepts optional parts and can easily be loaded onto a landship for transport, making it an overall high-performance machine.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        88: "A humanoid Walker Machine developed in the relatively early stages.\nAlthough its joints are somewhat fragile, its light weight makes it easy to handle, giving it excellent mobility and maneuverability. It also readily accepts optional parts and can easily be loaded onto a landship for transport, making it an overall high-performance machine.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        89: "A Walker Machine that enjoys enduring popularity among breakers.\nAs shown by the Napalm Guns mounted on both arms, ill-suited for excavation work, and its abundant fixed armament, it was developed purely for combat.\nDespite a build that gives an impression of sluggishness, it boasts high maneuverability. Its hover nozzles also allow for short-range flight, giving it more than adequate mobility as well.",
        90: "A Walker Machine that enjoys enduring popularity among breakers.\nAs shown by the Napalm Guns mounted on both arms, ill-suited for excavation work, and its abundant fixed armament, it was developed purely for combat.\nDespite a build that gives an impression of sluggishness, it boasts high maneuverability. Its hover nozzles also allow for short-range flight, giving it more than adequate mobility as well.",
        91: "A large Walker Machine that truly shows its worth in close-quarters combat.\nIts four-fingered structure, close to a human hand, gives it exceptionally high dexterity for work, a defining trait. This comes at the cost of a strong quirkiness that makes it difficult to handle, so it cannot be called widely popular. Even so, it leaves plenty of room for modification, making it a machine favored by connoisseurs who can bring out its potential through tuning.",
        92: "A large Walker Machine that truly shows its worth in close-quarters combat.\nThough a quirky machine that is difficult to handle, Timp pilots it with ease. This is also the unit used to kill Jiron's parents, and it was used again when Jiron himself came seeking revenge.\nTimp's personal mark is emblazoned on its hip joint.",
        93: "A Walker Machine that enjoys overwhelming support among breakers.\nIts maneuverability, provided by a high-output engine and hover nozzles, is exceptional. It is also a high-performance machine boasting heavy armor, ample fixed armament, and excellent habitability. However, its resulting high price is its greatest drawback.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        94: "A Walker Machine that enjoys overwhelming support among breakers.\nIts maneuverability, provided by a high-output engine and hover nozzles, is exceptional. It is also a high-performance machine boasting heavy armor, ample fixed armament, and excellent habitability. However, its resulting high price is its greatest drawback.\nIncidentally, Walker Machines come in a wide variety of color schemes largely because they tend to be the personal property of individual breakers, whose tastes and preferences vary widely.",
        95: "A Walker Machine specialized for flight capability.\nAttacks from the air using the two hover units mounted on its back overturned conventional wisdom about combat. Combined with the tremendous firepower concentrated at its front, it gave Jiron and his companions a great deal of trouble.\nIts legs are barely more than something to use when landing, making it a machine that can hardly be called a 'Walker Machine' anymore.",
        96: "A combat Walker Machine developed by the Innocent to arm their own agents.\nIt combines the strengths of both the Xabungle and the Walker Gallier, and by eliminating the transformation and combination mechanisms, it achieves improved maintainability and reliability. It also carries a large rotor on its back along with hover nozzles on its underside, giving it flight performance equal to or greater than that of the Walker Gallier.",
        97: "A Gavank-class landship.\nThough small, it offers high habitability. It more often serves as a hauler for transport and cargo work than as a combat vessel.",
        98: "A Midship-class landship.\nIt is equipped with a large crane called the 'Iron Arm' at its bow.\nIt is used mainly by mid-level haulers, and there are numerous variants, each modified independently by its owner.",
        99: "A Midship-class landship.\nIt has a hangar at the bow and a deck at the stern, giving it ample cargo space. It appears to be quite practical, and has become widely popular.",
        100: "An Emperor Custom-class landship.\nBuilt solely for combat, its distinguishing feature is a form rare among landships: aside from the area around the bridge, it is symmetrical both front-to-back and left-to-right.\nIt was operated by Houla in the decisive battle against the Civilians, and later by a mind-controlled Elche, waging fierce combat against the Iron Gear.",
        101: "The third of three landships built to the Iron Gear type. Its armor and output have been reinforced, making it the highest-performing of the three vessels.\nCommanded by a mind-controlled Elche, under the Innocent's influence, it challenged the Iron Gear, crewed by Jiron and his companions, to battle.",
        102: "The Walker Machine form of the Gear Gear.\nCommanded by Elche, brainwashed by the Innocent, it engaged in a fierce grappling battle against the Iron Gear, crewed by Jiron and his companions.",
        103: "A mobile suit independently developed by the Titans aboard Gryps I.\nIt is a redesign of the original Gundam, but by abolishing the Core Block System and adopting a Movable Frame, it achieves high maneuverability. New technologies are also incorporated throughout the airframe, including a linear-seat cockpit with a full panoramic monitor and a detachable Vulcan pod system.\nAfter it was seized from the Titans by Kamille and his allies, its color scheme was changed from black to white.\nBy combining with the later-developed G-Defenser, it became possible to boost firepower and armor and extend its cruising range.",
        104: "The state of the G-Defenser combined with the Gundam Mk-II's backpack area. Also called the Mk-II Defenser, it can also transform into its cruising form, the G-Flyer.\nAmid the astonishing pace at which mobile suit development was advancing, the performance gap of the Gundam Mk-II had already become pronounced, and these Parts were manufactured to power it up. With increased firepower, reinforced side and rear armor, and an enlarged backpack section that extends cruising range, its performance reaches a level that approaches even the Zeta Gundam. In particular, the G-Defenser's greatest weapon, the Long Beam Rifle, holds extraordinary destructive power even among firearms a mobile suit can carry.",
        105: "A mobile suit independently developed by the Titans aboard Gryps I.\nIt is a redesign of the original Gundam, but by abolishing the Core Block System and adopting a Movable Frame, it achieves high maneuverability. New technologies are also incorporated throughout the airframe, including a linear-seat cockpit with a full panoramic monitor and a detachable Vulcan pod system.\nFinished in the black-and-purple scheme also known as Titans colors, three units were produced. Emma served as test pilot for Unit 1, Kacricon for Unit 2, and Jerid for Unit 3.",
        106: "A variable mobile suit developed by Anaheim Electronics for the AEUG.\nThe crowning achievement of the know-how accumulated through the Zeta Project, it was completed by combining the Movable Frame technology from the Gundam Mk-II with the concept of the Flying Armor.\nBy adopting Gundarium gamma armor and a new-model generator, it achieves outstanding mobility. It can also make use of the Hyper Mega Launcher, a handheld weapon whose power rivals even that of the Mega Bazooka Launcher.\nBy further transforming into Waverider form, it displays tremendous cruising range and acceleration. Capable of standalone atmospheric reentry, independent flight within an atmosphere, and carrying an allied unit on its back during operations, it is a machine that can perform in virtually any situation.\nIt was later fitted with the Bio-Sensor, a simplified psycommu device, granting it responsiveness that keeps pace with Kamille's honed reflexes.",
        107: "The cruising form of the Zeta Gundam.\nIt can be used as an aerial and space fighter, or to carry an allied unit on its back, but its greatest feature is that it makes standalone atmospheric reentry possible.\nIt is called the Waverider because it derives lift from the compressed shock wave formed along the underside of its hull.",
        108: "A prototype mobile suit born from the AEUG's Zeta Project, developed by Anaheim Electronics.\nIt was originally one of the design candidates for the Zeta Gundam, but development was halted due to flaws in its variable mechanism, and it was later redesigned as a non-transforming unit. Its performance is high, and thanks in particular to its adoption of a Movable Frame and Wing Binders, it became a machine boasting maneuverability among the very best.\nIt has numerous conspicuous visual features, including its vivid gold body color and the character for 'hundred' emblazoned on both shoulders.",
        109: "The first mobile suit independently developed by 'Karaba,' an anti-Earth Federation organization sympathetic to the AEUG.\nA prototype developed with reference to the Rick Dias, provided by the AEUG, it achieves a high standard of maneuverability and mobility.\nPerhaps because a number of former Principality of Zeon engineers were involved in its development, traces of the MS-14 Gelgoog, mass-produced during the One Year War, can be seen in its head and close-combat armament.\nDeployed aboard the Audhumla, it has since become, in practice, Amuro Ray's personal unit.",
        110: "The AEUG's first original mobile suit, developed by Anaheim Electronics.\nDeveloped mainly by former Zeon engineers, it is notable for a silhouette resembling the MS-09 Dom. It was also the first machine to use Gundarium gamma in its armor, resulting in a substantial weight reduction compared to conventional mobile suits.\nIts red coloring was originally used only for Quattro's personal unit, but it later became the standard color. There is no difference in performance between the red and black colorings.",
        111: "The AEUG's first original mobile suit, developed by Anaheim Electronics.\nDeveloped mainly by former Zeon engineers, it is notable for a silhouette resembling the MS-09 Dom. It was also the first machine to use Gundarium gamma in its armor, resulting in a substantial weight reduction compared to conventional mobile suits.\nThe black coloring was used on units for ordinary soldiers, but all units were later repainted red, which became the standard color. There is no difference in performance between the two.",
    },
}
